<newsitem itemid="44461" id="root" date="1996-09-10" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Allied Leisure yr profits hit by exceptional.</title>
<headline>Allied Leisure yr profits hit by exceptional.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)(post-excep)1.40		   vs 2.44</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 0.5		    vs nil</p>
<p> Pretax, post-exceps    1.14		   vs 1.83</p>
<p> Turnover		   26.73		  vs 20.40</p>
<p> Operating result	 2.39		   vs 2.99</p>
<p> Exceptional		1.4		    vs nil</p>
<p> Interest receivable    0.12		   vs 0.03</p>
<p> Interest payable	 1.23		   vs 1.19</p>
<p> Tax			  0.21		   vs nil</p>
<p> Net taxed		  1.35		   vs 1.83</p>
<p> Pay date		   December 16</p>
<p> Div registration date  November 12</p>
<p> Ex-div date		November 4</p>
<p>Note - Allied Leisure Plc said the exceptional charge of 1.4 million stg related to the reorganisation of the GX Superbowl business bought from Granada in January 1996.</p>
<p>It said like-for-like sales in the first nine weeks of the current year were up 20 percent.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
